### noergler team self-service, IntelliJ HTTP client
# Pick an environment (dev / prod) from http-client.env.json and fill in host,
# team, secret and token there; do not commit secret or token.
#
# {{host}}    noergler base URL, e.g. https://noergler.example.com
# {{team}}    your team slug, as in teams.yaml
# {{secret}}  the team's webhook secret (from the noergler admin): authenticates every call
# {{token}}   your own Bitbucket HTTP access token with project admin: only for /onboard

### What the team has: claims and review author lists
GET {{host}}/teams/{{team}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secret}}

### Status of every claim: ownership, bot access, webhook state, stray repo hooks. No writes.
POST {{host}}/onboard/{{team}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secret}}
X-Bitbucket-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action": "status"}

### Claim a whole project and some repos of a shared one, create the hooks, grant the bot write access
POST {{host}}/onboard/{{team}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secret}}
X-Bitbucket-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "grant-bot",
  "projects": [
    {"key": "PLAT"},
    {"key": "INFRA", "repos": ["terraform-core", "ansible"]}
  ]
}

### Same, but only report what would happen (no claim, no hook, no grant)
POST {{host}}/onboard/{{team}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secret}}
X-Bitbucket-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "grant-bot",
  "dry_run": true,
  "projects": [{"key": "PLAT"}]
}

### Re-run the hooks over the current claims (after a webhook secret rotation: remove first, see below)
POST {{host}}/onboard/{{team}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secret}}
X-Bitbucket-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action": "grant-bot"}

### Give a repo up: hook, claim and every review record of it go. Count first.
POST {{host}}/onboard/{{team}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secret}}
X-Bitbucket-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "remove",
  "dry_run": true,
  "projects": [{"key": "INFRA", "repos": ["ansible"]}]
}

### ... then for real
POST {{host}}/onboard/{{team}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secret}}
X-Bitbucket-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "remove",
  "projects": [{"key": "INFRA", "repos": ["ansible"]}]
}

### Remove the hooks only (claims and data stay), e.g. before a secret rotation
POST {{host}}/onboard/{{team}}
Authorization: Bearer {{secret}}
X-Bitbucket-Token: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action": "remove"}

### Who gets automatic reviews (empty = everyone) and who never triggers one (CI and dependency bots)
PUT {{host}}/teams/{{team}}/review-authors
Authorization: Bearer {{secret}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "auto_review_authors": [],
  "ignore_authors": ["ci-bot", "renovate"]
}
